1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,148
Here combines photo based indoor localization with visual route guidance.

2
00:00:06,017 --> 00:00:08,992
COLMAP builds a sparse map from a phone video.

3
00:00:08,992 --> 00:00:13,131
Reference cameras share one three dimensional coordinate system.

4
00:00:14,017 --> 00:00:15,709
Upload a corridor photo.

5
00:00:15,709 --> 00:00:22,477
Feature matching and two D to three D registration estimate the camera position and orientation.

6
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:25,853
These are genuine model coordinates.

7
00:00:25,853 --> 00:00:30,303
Metric distances require a measured scale, and are not invented.

8
00:00:31,183 --> 00:00:32,535
Choose a destination.

9
00:00:32,535 --> 00:00:35,947
A star search follows the connected navigation graph.

10
00:00:35,947 --> 00:00:40,003
Turn directions come from the camera heading and route vectors.

11
00:00:40,892 --> 00:00:45,084
A perspective style arrow is drawn on the localization photo.

12
00:00:45,084 --> 00:00:48,794
Stored reference images illustrate the upcoming steps.

13
00:00:49,683 --> 00:00:51,765
Re-localize to update progress.

14
00:00:51,765 --> 00:00:59,219
For this controlled arrival check, we replay a registered waypoint image, then let the program confirm arrival.

15
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:04,232
This is a real photo replay, not live augmented reality.

16
00:01:04,232 --> 00:01:07,479
On site walking validation is the next step.
